trength","location":"Iron Island","obtained":"Gift from Riley","changed":false},{"tm":"HM05","move":"Defog","location":"Solaceon Ruins","obtained":"Item on ground","changed":false},{"tm":"HM06","move":"Rock Smash","location":"Oreburgh Gate","obtained":"Gift from NPC","changed":false},{"tm":"HM07","move":"Waterfall","location":"Pastoria Gym","obtained":"Gift from Wake","changed":true},{"tm":"HM08","move":"Rock Climb","location":"Snowpoint City","obtained":"Gift from Candice","changed":true}],"vitaminReplacements":["- HP Up >> Focus Sash","- Protein >> Enigma Berry","- Iron >> Sitrus Berry","- Calcium >> Power Herb","- Zinc >> Chesto Berry","- Carbos >> White Herb"],"plateLocations":["Draco Plate: Celestic Town - Ruins","Dread Plate: Sendoff Spring - Entrance","Earth Plate: Oreburgh Gate - 1F","Fist Plate: Veilstone City - Massager's House","Flame Plate: Route 226 - Survival Area side","Icicle Plate: Snowpoint City - Right of Gym","Insect Plate: Route 202 - South on route","Iron Plate: Iron Island - Outside entrance to cave","Meadow Plate: Floaroma Meadow - Right of house","Mind Plate: Solaceon Ruins - Entrance","Sky Plate: Pokémon League - Right of League entrance","Splash Plate: Route 219 - Sandgem side","Spooky Plate: Lost Tower - 1F","Stone Plate: Route 207 - Above mud slide to the right","Toxic Plate: Great Marsh - Upstairs observatory","Zap Plate: Sunyshore City - Lighthouse"],"replacedItems":[{"oldItem":"Contest Pass","newItem":"Ice Stone"},{"oldItem":"Coupon 1","newItem":"Red Orb"},{"oldItem":"Coupon 2","newItem":"Blue Orb"},{"oldItem":"Coupon 3","newItem":"Jade Orb"},{"oldItem":"Loot Sack","newItem":"Prism Scale"},{"oldItem":"Point Card","newItem":"Silver Wing"},{"oldItem":"Rule Book","newItem":"Rainbow Wing"},{"oldItem":"S.S. Ticket","newItem":"Tea"},{"oldItem":"Seal Bag","newItem":"GS Ball","note":"*"},{"oldItem":"Storage Key","newItem":"Mysterious Invitation","note":"**"},{"oldItem":"Old Rod","newItem":"Worm Lure"},{"oldItem":"Good Rod","newItem":"Berry Lure"},{"oldItem":"Super Rod","newItem":"Fish Lure"}],"noteSections":[{"title":"Modified Items","lines":["The following items now have a \"Use\" option like evolutionary stones:","The following items have had adjustments to their costs:","The following items now cost zero and are thus unsellable:"]},{"title":"Modified TMs","lines":["The following TMs have had their moves changed (compatibility matches Ultra Sun and Ultra Moon plus extras as listed in Pokémon Changes):","TM41: Torment >> Hydro Pump","TM47: Steel Wing >> Iron Head","TM55: Brine >> Scald","TM57: Charge Beam >> Wild Charge","TM62: Silver Wind >> Bug Buzz","TM72: Avalanche >> Icicle Crash","TM83: Natural Gift >> Hyper Voice","TM85: Dream Eater >> Dazzling Gleam","TM88: Pluck >> Hurricane","Additionally, all TMs will now have a quantity of 99 when obtained.","No TMs are available within Poké Marts.","An NPC at the Pokémon League can reset your inventory to have 99 of all TMs."]},{"title":"Poké Mart Inventory","lines":["Poké Marts have had a small universal inventory change."]},{"title":"TM Locations","lines":["A * means the location has changed from the original Platinum."]},{"title":"Vitamin Replacements","lines":["Since Effort Values(EVs) have been removed, this means that vitamins have been removed, as well.","Each vitamin has been replaced with a corresponding consumable item.","Because hidden items are handled differently than visible ones, and no one has made a script editor capable of editing the global scripts that decide which","item you get from them, the hidden vitamins have instead been removed(placed so far off the map that they're unobtainable).","PP Up and PP Max are unchanged, as they have nothing to do with Effort Values.","(Power items and Vitamins are still obtainable in the Battle Frontier, as these cannot be edited. The Battle Frontier itself is currently impossible to edit with my knowledge.)"]},{"title":"Plate Locations","lines":["The sixteen Arceus plates (Pixie Plate was not added) have all been removed from their normal locations.","You can get them either from the Underground or defeating the Master Trainer of that type.","Master Trainers will appear after speaking to the old lady in the Foreign Building in Hearthome after becoming Champion."]},{"title":"Replaced Items","lines":["The following items (some unobtainable) have been replaced with items from other games.","Items under the \"Old Item\" column are now unavailable.","The fishing rod items have been replaced with new lure","items that can be used to catch different Pokémon.","They are used in the same way.","Lure: Worm","A lure resembling a worm, to be used with your fishing rod.","This lure will attract unfinicky Pokémon.","Lure: Berry","A lure resembling a berry, to be used with your fishing rod.","This lure will attract gentle Pokémon.","Lure: Fish","A lure resembling a fish, to be used with your fishing rod.","This lure will attract aggressive Pokémon.","* Thank you to Serebii.net for the item sprite.","** A completely new item that is used in the Mewtwo event."]}]}
